{
  "cites": "a hello the Guardian answered with SESSION_REFUSED, followed by the startup posture applied as though nothing had answered: the session started and the deployment log records an unguarded start. A refusal is a decision, and section 4.1 applies the posture only when no answer arrives, so the session is refused with the code the Guardian sent. A checker that looks only for the deployment-log record passes this member, and so does an Observed Agent that reads every error without a ServerHello as an outage.",
